  "query_preview": "..\n\nLight winds and patchy morning fog are expected Wednesday morning,\nespecially in the river valleys. Otherwise, look for temperatures\nin the 20s and 30s to start the day.\n\nUpper ridging will gradually progress eastward through the week\nhelping to maintain mainly dry and seasonable weather conditions.\nAn upper trough will push through the region on Friday with a cold\nfront Friday night and Saturday. For now, ensembles keep much of\nthe precipitation chances off to the south and west of the CWA.\n\nUpper ridging looks to rebound over the weekend. Look for largely\ndry weather and warming temperatures under the larger scale\nsubsidence as high temperatures by Sunday reach into the 50s and \n60s.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nNo major deviations to NBM were used for this forecast cycle.\nThere remains low confidence on patchy fog for Wednesday morning.\nOtherwise there is strong consensus in support of mostly dry and\nseasonable weather through the week.",
